#!/bin/sh
# Claude Code hook (ai-dotfiles claude/settings.json): records Claude's state on its tmux pane, as
# pane options @claude (working or waiting) and @claude_since (epoch seconds), for the `ws` picker.
#
#   claude-tmux-status working|waiting   set the state; since only moves when the state changes
#   claude-tmux-status clear             Claude is exiting
#
# Always exits 0: a failing hook shows an error notice in Claude.

[ -n "$TMUX_PANE" ] || exit 0

case "$1" in
  clear)
    tmux set -pu -t "$TMUX_PANE" @claude \; set -pu -t "$TMUX_PANE" @claude_since
    ;;
  working | waiting)
    [ "$(tmux show -pqv -t "$TMUX_PANE" @claude)" = "$1" ] && exit 0
    tmux set -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" @claude "$1" \; set -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" @claude_since "$(date +%s)"
    ;;
esac >/dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
